"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify, in the rubric body, CI-agnostic DEFINITIONS (and abstract, non-vendor-named example shapes) of 'hard-fail step / required gate' and 'if-present/grandfather guard' so the LLM can recognize them without the banned CI-vendor keywords, and confirm the ban in AC line 3 does not starve the rubric of the anchors its decision rule needs.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.365,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: rubric 'asks a CI-agnostic question: \"does this pipeline/gate-configuration change introduce a hard-fail step or required gate with no if-present/grandfather guard, so a branch created before this change would fail?\"' — the single decision sentence, with no definition of 'hard-fail step', 'required gate', or 'grandfather/if-present guard'.","AC line 3 forbids the rubric BODY from containing any of the seven CI-vendor names case-insensitively, removing the natural concrete anchors an LLM would use to recognize these constructs across providers.","grep 'grandfather'/'if-present' across .rebar and docs finds no prior definition of these as recognition concepts — they are novel to this plan (the only 'grandfather' hits are the phase-boundaries suggested_fix corpus, an unrelated sense).","Contrast: .rebar/prompts/code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries.md defines its full vocabulary in-body (the four passes + each phase's owned actions + explicit 'Do not flag' list), which is what lets its LLM abstain correctly; the new rubric's spec has no analogous in-body definition of its recognition terms."],"finding":"The rubric's decision rule depends on three load-bearing recognition concepts — 'hard-fail step', 'required gate', and 'if-present/grandfather guard' — that the plan neither defines nor illustrates, while AC line 3 bans every concrete CI-vendor anchor from the rubric BODY; the executor-LLM is thus given an undefined vocabulary and no CI-agnostic recognition pattern for what a guarded vs. ungrandfathered gate looks like.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f551f0c6e8aad5208","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (rubric decision question) + Acceptance Criteria line 3 (body contains none of github/gitlab/jenkins/circleci/buildkite/bitbucket/drone) + .rebar/prompts/code-review-project-ci-gate-compat.md","norm_id":"nf04cb1aa0e54e23b","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A gitlab-ci.yml diff adds a `rules:` guard vs. an unconditional required job — the LLM must decide 'is this a grandfather guard?' with no defined criterion.","A .github/workflows change adds a new required check with `if: hashFiles(...)` — is that an if-present guard? The rubric gives no anchor to decide, especially with vendor keywords banned from its own text."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the rubric, add a short 'What counts' section defining the constructs abstractly (e.g. 'a hard-fail step = a pipeline step whose non-zero exit fails the whole run and is not conditioned on the changed artifact existing; a grandfather/if-present guard = a condition that skips or soft-passes the step when its target file/branch predates the change'), using vendor-neutral phrasing so AC line 3's ban still holds, and mirror the phase-boundaries rubric's explicit 'Do not flag' list.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitiga